claim.claim-text:
13. An isolated or recombinantly produced polypeptide selected from the group consisting of: a) a polypeptide having lipid A biosynthesis acyltransferase activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 70% 

identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by nucleotides 350-1234 (ORF 2a) of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1 ; b) a polypeptide having glycosyltransferase activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 70%> identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by nucleotides 1234-2487 (ORF 3a) of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1 ; c) a polypeptide having glycosyltransferase activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 50 % identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by nucleotides 2786-3952 (ORF 4a) of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1 over a region at least about 100 amino acids in length; d) a polypeptide having β 1 ,4-GalNAc transferase activity, wherein the GalNAc transferase polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 11% identical to an amino acid sequence as set forth in SΕQ ID NO: 13 over a region at least about 50 amino acids in length; e) a polypeptide having β 1 ,3-galactosyltransferase activity, wherein the galactosyltransferase polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 75% identical to an amino acid sequence as set forth in SΕQ ID NO: 15 or SΕQ ID NO: 17 over a region at least about 50 amino acids in length; f) a polypeptide having α2,3 sialyltransferase activity, wherein the sialyltransferase polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 66% identical to an amino acid sequence as set forth in SΕQ ID NO: 3, SΕQ ID NO: 5, SΕQ ID NO: 7 or SΕQ ID NO: 10 over a region at least about 60 amino acids in length; g) a polypeptide having sialic acid synthase activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 70% identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by nucleotides 6924-7961 of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1 ; h) a polypeptide having sialic acid biosynthesis activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 70% identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by nucleotides 8021 -9076 of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1 ; 

 i) a polypeptide having CMP-sialic acid synthetase activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 65 %> identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by nucleotides 9076-9738 of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1 ; j) a polypeptide having acetyltransferase activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 65% identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by nucleotides 9729-10559 of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1 ; and k) a polypeptide having glycosyltransferase activity, wherein the polypeptide comprises an amino acid sequence that is at least about 65 %> identical to an amino acid sequence encoded by a reverse complement of nucleotides 10557-11366 of the EOS biosynthesis locus of C. jejuni strain ΟH4384 as shown in SΕQ ID NO: 1.
